{
  "esm": "0.4.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "gradient_duo_pde",
    "description": "C-grid normal gradient d(g)/dt = grad(q, dim=edge) on a DUO icosahedral triangular mesh. q is the cell-centered scalar; g is the edge-normal gradient output (edge-located, shape [n_edges]). Lowered from gradient_duo (Heikes et al. 2023): (grad q)_e = (q[faces_on_edge[e,2]] - q[faces_on_edge[e,1]]) / dv_edge[e]. The cell field q is injected at bind time by the unstructured-gradient Layer-B runner; the q tendency is frozen (zero) so one RHS evaluation yields the discrete edge-normal gradient of the prescribed scalar field."
  },
  "models": {
    "M": {
      "grid": "domain",
      "variables": {
        "g": { "type": "state", "shape": ["n_edges"], "location": "edge_normal", "default": 0.0 },
        "q": { "type": "state", "shape": ["n_cells"], "location": "cell_center", "default": 0.0 }
      },
      "equations": [
        { "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["g"], "wrt": "t" }, "rhs": { "op": "grad", "args": ["q"], "dim": "edge" } },
        { "lhs": { "op": "D", "args": ["q"], "wrt": "t" }, "rhs": 0.0 }
      ],
      "time": { "t0": 0.0, "t_final": 0.001 }
    }
  }
}
